From 9e16733617a47f647ed91ef98f62994bf3580d12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CrockMr <118761873+CrockMr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:25:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Report a captive job's goal as the state 0.5 goal of its
 worker

MeitouClient runs captive work (gathering slaves from cages, working them, getting into a cage...)
as CaptiveSystem jobs. The AI holds no worker of a job, so its mind keeps the goal it had before,
and state 0.5 reported that stale goal: a slaver read stay_in_home while it gathered or worked
slaves, where the original's census shows gather_slaves_from_cages or work_the_slaves.

The captive sweep now records on each job the AI goal it started the job for (CaptiveJob.Goal, a
role list's or the race's). While a job runs, the worker's 0.5 goal is that goal, by row number
with its tier; otherwise it is the mind's goal as before. 0.1 to 0.4 output is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
